## TIER — TIER 1, argued (the drafter's reading; Tuesday confirms at stamp)
**Tiers:** full weight (TIER 1) for security surfaces, data destruction, deploys and human handovers; through-code only for tests/docs/config/already-gated follow-ups.
**The case FOR through-code:** RD-848 is the follow-up of gate 23's own finding F-846-1; the removed line sits in the `build` stage, which does not ship; the shipped `/app` is predicted unchanged; the rest of the diff is test code and a counts file.
**Why that loses — TIER 1:** (1) the `Dockerfile` IS the deploy recipe: `.github/workflows/deploy-demo.yml` (unchanged by this diff, READ ONLY) runs `az acr build` on **every push to main** when the repo variable `CI_DEPLOY_ENABLED` is `true`, then deploys — merging this branch can build and roll the demo image without a human step (the variable's live value is UNKNOWN to the drafter); (2) the defect class (an empty layer that makes ACR's naive-diff builder fail a LATER `COPY`) is invisible to jest, to overlay2 and to Docker Desktop — it is measurable only at the image level, so a through-code gate would pass without testing the thing; (3) RD-846's own history: one such line blocked the owed demo deploy and every release image; (4) the new guard is a **CHECKER** (template §2a applies) whose false negatives would re-open exactly that door. "Already-gated follow-up" does not apply: gate 23 gated RD-846, never this diff. **Image legs are required; the verdict is PROVISIONAL without them.**

