## 2. Tier and severity rules
**TIER 1:** at the head, ANY COPY step in ANY stage that records no layer on vfs (the census) is a **Major** (the shape RD-848 exists to remove), and a **Blocker** if it fails a build; P-base NOT failing on vfs makes r1 **VOID** for the head's green (the daemon cannot see the shape) — never a pass; P-head FAILING on vfs is a **Blocker**; M-readd848 not failing makes C-76's red proof **UNVERIFIED** (a **Major** against the READY's cause); ANY production `/app` difference between base and head images (path, type, uid:gid, mode, sha256, symlink target, any `node_modules` entry) not explained by a build arg is a **Blocker**; `/app/package.json` or `/app/package-lock.json` not byte-identical to git's `384805d` / `19477a9` is a **Blocker**; the build stage at head not holding the pair (byte-identical) or not running is a **Major**; the head image not starting, or `build` ≠ `15f6e1debe3ac6c5` for a correctly-argued build, is a **Blocker**; an image-reading cell red at head, or a base test name absent at head, is a **Major**; a Dockerfile non-comment change beyond the one removed line is a **Major**; a guard claim that is FALSE as worded is a **Minor** (a **Major** if the guard is green on a shape that fails a vfs build AND the live file carries that shape); a guard clause no cell kills (a surviving mutant) is a **Minor**; a planted control that does not fire makes its row **VOID**, never a pass; a false READY claim is a **Minor**; a NEW CodeQL-shaped pattern in the changed JS (both thresholds, by pattern) is a **NOTE** naming the pattern (the PR run decides). **Severity is yours; priority is Tuesday's.** **Who is waiting:** merge author **NexusAI-O (S100O)**, then any release image from main.

