## 2b. THE GUARD IS A CHECKER — its legitimate shapes, and every READY claim as a check that CAN FAIL
**The ordinary shapes the guard will see in service, legitimate first (each must be GREEN), then the defect shapes (each must be RED).** Run each through `analyse()` / `redundantCopies()` in YOUR head tree (belted, a scratch driver in YOUR evidence dir, never committed):

| shape — as a builder really produces it | expected verdict | the helper clause that yields it | predicted-by |
|---|---|---|---|
| a new `COPY newdir/ ./newdir/` of files no stage holds | green (`new`) | `writes.every(held)` false | drafter |
| `COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules` (RUN output) | `not-modelled`, never redundant | `unmodelled` branch, `:224`, `:239` | READY |
| a re-copy with `--chown=node:node` of the held pair | green | `meta` in the identity, `:214` | READY |
| a new root `*.js` file picked up by `COPY *.js ./` beside the held `model-config.js` (line 53 then 54) | green | one changed file suffices | drafter |
| the base-stage pair through a glob (`COPY package*.json ./`) followed by the named pair in build (8de8e5c) | **RED** on the build line | glob resolution `:96-108` | READY |
| the RD-846 line restored in production / the RD-848 line restored in build | **RED**, naming the stage | inheritance `:176` | READY |
| a byte-identical re-copy spelled with the DEFAULT owner (`--chown=0:0`) | the READY's model says green; **the real layer is empty** | textual `meta` | drafter (WRONG 6) |

**Each READY claim → a check that CAN FAIL, with its positive and negative control:**
- **C1 "19 cells, 19/19 green at head; 7 of 19 red at 17fc6c5's Dockerfile, each naming `Dockerfile:74 (stage build)`."** Check: run the rd848 suite at head (r5) AND with the head's helper+test over the BASE Dockerfile (a scratch tree = head + base `Dockerfile` blob `4e5638e`). FAIL if head < 19/19, or the base-Dockerfile run is not red, or any red names a line other than 74. Positive control = the base-Dockerfile run's reds; negative control = the head run's greens.
- **C2 "real trees: 0677388, 1fd5d0f, 7c47ec4, b2fc9bf GREEN; 8de8e5c, 4016ba5, 3f7e263, e224ab9, 3907c57 RED on build + production; 3a45914, 17fc6c5 RED on build only."** Check: YOUR driver calls the head helper's `commitContext(sha)` + `redundantCopies` on each sha in YOUR clone (never the builder's `rd848-real-trees.js` in place). FAIL on any mismatch. Positive control: 8de8e5c red (the glob shape); negative: 7c47ec4 green.
