## 3a. INSTRUMENT RULES — H-1..H-35 carried from gate 23's brief §3a (which carries gate 22's), re-based to gate 24
**Read gate 22's §3a WHOLE at `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/briefs/2026-10-13_nexusai-gate-batch22.md` and gate 23's §3a at `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/briefs/2026-10-16_nexusai-gate-batch23.md`, and apply every rule** (their member-specific examples do not apply). Restated where they bind this gate:
- **H-1.** The ONLY permitted SESSION_SECRET printer, verbatim:
  `if [ -n "${SESSION_SECRET+x}" ]; then echo "SESSION_SECRET SET (length ${#SESSION_SECRET})"; else echo "SESSION_SECRET UNSET"; fi`.
  **FORBIDDEN:** `${SESSION_SECRET-…}`, `${SESSION_SECRET:-…}`, `${SESSION_SECRET+$SESSION_SECRET}`, `echo $SESSION_SECRET`, `printenv`, `env | grep`, `set | grep`, an echoed env array (`${envs[*]}`), and unscanned `docker inspect` output (T3). Self-test the printer and the scan before the first hold (the scan's control plants a DIFFERENT marker); after every hold and r3 run report the throwaway's count (0); needles printed only as `<first4>…<last4>`. **Never copy gate 23's `inst/.throwaway-ss`.**
- **H-3** a LANDING CONTROL for every hook (a probe present in YOUR commit AND in the packed tar's member bytes; each daemon reports the driver asked for). **H-4** the heartbeat is a **separate child**, the hold aborted if no HB **within 90 s** of the grant, the **max gap** reported (≤ 120 s). **H-6** every path quoted (`!CODING`, spaces — gate 23 §14 item 2 lost a run to an unquoted `Testing Agent MAIN`); every host jest run but the full verifies, every driver and script under `qa-netbelt.sb` with its landing control. **H-7/H-8** mutants by a quoted tool with a negative control; landed = "the exact mutated text is present AND the original text is absent once the new text is removed"; **an edit whose anchor is absent FAILS LOUDLY and nothing downstream runs on that tree** (gate 23 §14 item 4 packed an UNMUTATED tree under a mutant's name). **H-9** byte plants by `Buffer`, checked by `xxd -l 16` and `wc -c`, never `echo`/`printf`/heredoc/`JSON.stringify`. **H-11/H-18** `/bin/bash` explicitly, `"${sha}:${path}"` (zsh eats `:s`/`:a`; a bare `=====` line is a zsh error); a sha256 of `e3b0c442…` is a VOID read. **H-14** every driver ends `END ok` or `END VOID <reason>`. **H-17** absolute tool paths; assert each arm STARTED (`Step 1/`, `docker info`, jest's first suite, the listen line); censuses by `pgrep`, never `/bin/ps` (setuid). **H-21** every mutated file restored by a `trap … EXIT` (INT, TERM) installed BEFORE the first mutation, hash-compared to its pin (`Dockerfile` head `f0367f1`, helper head blob read at start). **H-22** never nest `sandbox-exec` (it exits 71). **H-24** jest ARRAY options after the paths; lists built in bash; PASS/FAIL lines = list length. **H-26** ls-remote retried 5 × ~10 s on `Permission denied (publickey)`; a failure is UNKNOWN. **H-27** THE MODEL RULE. **H-29** gate 23's and the builder's evidence is METHOD only. **H-31** §1's offline install; never `npm install`, `npm update`, `npm audit`, a downloading `npx`. **H-33** plants, contexts, exports, listings, env files and scratch repos only in YOUR dirs; every child counted by pid and reaped (C-174); **never `rm` — quarantine** (gate 23 §14 item 5: an `rmdir` of an empty dir is still a removal).
- **H-20 (deadlines, `qa-to.sh`, rc 142 = fired):** targeted cells 600 s, each full verify 2,400 s, offline npm ci 600 s, each docker build 1,200 s, each dind start 120 s, each container boot + health read 180 s, each context pack 300 s, each `az` call 900 s. A fired deadline ABORTS that step, named, never silently retried.
- **H-28 (AMENDED).** **A hold never idles holding a lock**; ONE focused hold at a time ACROSS BOTH KINDS, ≤ ~40 minutes planned; every part file written and `bash -n`-checked BEFORE filing; you stay in the FOREGROUND (a long command is a TRACKED child, never `nohup`, its timeout the 2-hour maximum, polled in the foreground); wait deadline = 2 h − (planned + 15 min), and BEFORE it fires, `--replace` your own waiting ticket under the SAME tag. **Your filer is a COPY of gate 23's `qa-file23.sh`, re-pointed to `qa-g24-<HOLD>` and to `docker` or `jest`.** **READ YOUR INBOX before filing every new hold** (gate 23 §14 item 8 filed D3 after an unread "no new legs"). **Suggested grouping:** **D1 (docker) = r1** (vfs: base, head, P-base, P-head, M-readd848 + census; overlay2: P-base control) — about 7 builds, SPLIT into D1a/D1b if over ~40 min; **D2 (docker) = r2 + r6** (overlay2: base/head production + `--target build`, plants (ii)/(iii); vfs: M-chown0, M-sameBytes); **D3 (docker) = r3** (+ T1's ACR legs if decided, under the same docker lock); **H1 (jest) = r5 + §2b** (TIER 1, the first jest hold); **H2 (jest) = r4 head** + ruling (n)'s control pair; **H3 (jest) = r4 base**. r0, r7, r8, r9's decision, the context packs, §2b's static checks (C2, C3, C10) and every READ are lock-free.
