## 9. Floor discipline — MERGES GO FIRST, both locks, THE DEADLINE RULE
1. **MERGES GO FIRST (ruling i) — NO BY-HAND YIELD.** The jest AND docker lock `session-tools/nexusai-lock.sh` (`<jest|docker> <tag> [--replace <own-ticket>] <cmd…>`; queues `queue-jest/` and `queue-docker/` under the T9 base) is shared with the builder seats. **Do ALL lock-free work first** (pins, hashes, reads, r0, the context packs, r7, r8, the offline `npm ci`, §2b C2/C3/C10). **Then file your holds ONE AT A TIME**, tagged `qa-g24-…` (e.g. `qa-g24-D1a`, `qa-g24-H1`), each a tracked child, through the INSTALLED tool; a ticket queued AHEAD of you is waited behind (FIFO); at a wait deadline, `--replace`; **once granted, carry on.** **QUEUE, NEVER TAKE OVER:** never kill, signal, move or edit another seat's process, lock, owner file, ticket, container or image.
2. **Hold a lock for a planned block of work, never idle (H-28).**
3. **Count foreign servers and seats the C-125 way, anchored on YOUR OWN claude pid; the NEGATIVE controls (all must classify FOREIGN in the same run) are the claude pids the launcher DERIVED LIVE — the coordinator pane, every live `Datasec/NexusAI-*` pane, `fleet-monitor` if a claude runs under it, every live peer `QA/*` pane — listed at the end of your prompt.** Re-read them at every hold's start (gate 23: the coordinator's pid changed mid-gate); **a hold with NO live negative control aborts.** Reuse `qa-floorlib23.sh` BY COPY with YOUR pid as `ROOT` and these as `NEG`, and `qa-floorcount.py`. Record the foreign RUNNING container set (`docker ps`) beside every docker result.
4. **A zero is reportable only beside a control that fired in the same window** — "empty diff" (r2's planted controls), "0 no-layer COPY" (the base census's one), the head's vfs PASS (P-base's FAIL), "LOST 0" (the base names), "guarded by no cell" (the mutant LANDED).
5. **THE LOAD RULE (Tuesday's 2026-10-17 ANSWER to S100O, `briefs/2026-10-17_nexusai-rd848-plan-ANSWER.txt`):** build images and run a full verify only below a 1-minute load of **40**; record `uptime` beside every hold's start. Above it, wait in the queue, never in a hold.

**6. THE DEADLINE RULE** — every step has a written DEADLINE (H-20), a HEARTBEAT line at least every **2 minutes** in a hold, a step silent for **5 minutes** is aborted and reported, every child is killed in a `finally` by pid from your own ancestry, never by pattern (C-174); your containers are stopped by ID.

